+# Homepage paint monitoring
+
+`performance-monitor.js` observes browser-reported contentful paints caused by
+navigation links, Order Now, and Seasonal Favorites cards (including their View
+Details links). It does not intercept clicks or change navigation behavior.
+
+Read the latest 100 reports with `window.dailyGrindPerformance.getReports()` or
+subscribe before interacting:
+
+```js
+window.addEventListener('daily-grind:performance', ({ detail }) => {
+  // Forward detail to your analytics integration here.
+});
+```
+
+No analytics requests are sent by this implementation. Reports contain stable
+control identifiers and labels, not DOM elements. Soft-navigation URLs are reduced
+to their pathname to omit query strings and fragments.
+
+- `interaction-paint`: `control`, `label`, `interactionId`, `startTime`, and
+  `duration` in milliseconds from interaction start to contentful presentation.
+  Each `phase: 'candidate'` report represents a progressively larger contentful
+  paint caused by that interaction, including asynchronous updates. It is not an
+  assertion that all network work or animations have finished.
+- `soft-navigation`: browser-detected client-side view switches, including
+  `path`, `navigationId`, `interactionId`, `fcpDuration`, `lcpDuration`, and
+  `lcpSize`. Durations are milliseconds relative to the initiating interaction,
+  not document load. `lcpDuration` is null when no candidate is available. A
+  `phase: 'final'` report is emitted on the next soft navigation, tab hide, or
+  pagehide, after draining pending observer records. Paints before URL changes
+  are seeded from `getLargestInteractionContentfulPaint()`; subsequent paints
+  are matched using `interactionId`.
+
+These APIs are experimental and not available in every browser. Check
+`window.dailyGrindPerformance.support`; unsupported observers are skipped. Click
+attribution additionally requires Event Timing; the browser may omit fast events
+below its minimum 16 ms threshold. An interaction without an attributed contentful
+paint produces no interaction report. No guessed timing fallback is emitted.
+
+The current homepage uses full-document navigation. This script measures visual
+updates in this document, and automatically observes soft navigations if
+client-side routing is introduced. It cannot measure destination-page painting
+after a full-document navigation or updates in another tab. Changing only a URL
+does not count as completing a visual update.
+
+Run `npm test` for the isolated observer and lifecycle tests. These tests use
+mocked browser APIs; they do not establish real browser support or paint accuracy.
